================================================================================
## Keep Initialize DML running when the app SP cannot apply DDL
================================================================================

Context:
Reliance (0.8.1) cannot Initialize because Lakebase tables are owned by a
provisioning service principal. schema.sql raises "must be owner of table"
and that failure aborted the DML that pins catalog/schema/volume, returning
502. Document reads in 0.9.0 go through the Lakebase Knowledge Store, so the
OntoBricksRegistry volume fallback on generate is not required here.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/Bootstrap.py
   Treat `_apply_ddl()` as non-fatal; log a warning and still upsert the
   registry row. DML failures still fail Initialize.
2. tests/units/registry/test_v090_lakebase_bootstrap.py
   Cover the non-owner DDL path and keep Initialize failing only on DML.

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/Bootstrap.py
- tests/units/registry/test_v090_lakebase_bootstrap.py
- changelogs/v0.9.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-10-12.log

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → 9001 passed, 326 skipped,
6 deselected, 1 xfailed, 40 warnings in 60.65s.
